    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225-a1">

                <pb facs="d225-03" n="3" xml:id="d225-03"/>

                <head>Tab A<lb/>Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Kissinger) to Secretary of State Rogers</head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1971-04-28">April 28, 1971</date></dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Negotiation of a Convention Banning Biological and Toxin Weapons</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has reviewed your memorandum of April 23, 1971, regarding
                    negotiation of a convention banning biological and toxin weapons at the
                    Conference of the Committee on Disarmament at Geneva, and approves moving ahead
                    promptly.</p>
                <p>A status report on developments in these negotiations should be forwarded to the
                    President periodically. If the need for changes in the U.S. position should
                    arise, hey must be approved by the President.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Henry A. Kissinger</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
